course: dictionary
lesson: 3763
title: Foamy: full of bubbles
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Foamy describes something covered in foam, or full of tiny bubbles. You can have «foamy milk» with bubbles on top, or «foamy waves» that froth white at the edge of the sea. The -y ending turns foam into a describing word, like sandy or bubbly.
explain: Read this sentence: «Sometimes a hedgehog chews something with a new smell and spreads foamy spit all over its spines.» The words around foamy are your clues: the hedgehog spreads the spit on its spines, so foamy must describe the spit. Check your meaning by swapping it in: full of bubbles still makes sense.
explain: Scientists call this self-anointing, and they are still not sure why hedgehogs do it. You do not need to know everything about a topic to understand the word. The sentence tells you what foamy means.
fact: Foamy means covered with foam or full of tiny bubbles.
fact: Foam is a mass of tiny bubbles, like the froth on a milkshake or in a bath.
fact: «Foamy bubbles» and «foamy milk» are common phrases.
fact: In science, foams show air trapped in a liquid.
fact: Mixing baking soda and vinegar makes a foamy reaction.
exercise: What does foamy mean? | Dark and cold | Very hot and steaming | *Covered with foam or full of tiny bubbles | Hard as a rock
exercise: «Sometimes a hedgehog spreads foamy spit all over its spines.» What does foamy describe? | The night | The spines | The hedgehog's smell | *The spit
exercise: Which of these is a foamy thing? | A dry biscuit | *A bath full of bubbly foam | A closed door | A cold stone
test: «Foamy waves» crashed onto the beach. What does foamy mean here? | Calm and flat | Frozen solid | Very loud | *Covered with white bubbles
test: Mixing baking soda and vinegar makes a foamy reaction. What happens? | *Bubbles form and froth up | The mixture turns solid | The liquid freezes | Everything goes dark
exam: Hannah says foamy is just a fancy word for wet. Which answer is best? | Yes, foamy and wet mean exactly the same | No, foamy means very old | *No, foamy means covered with foam or full of tiny bubbles | Yes, but only for water
